    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nTraditional detached farmhouse, set on 0.81 of an acre approximately, enjoying an exceptional and scenic setting between Glengarriff and Kenmare. Nestled in one of West Cork's most spectacular locations, the property offers a rare combination of privacy, character and breathtaking natural surroundings, while being just a 12-minute drive from the picturesque village of Glengarriff, renowned for its stunning harbour, vibrant community, and unrivalled natural beauty.\n\nThe accommodation is arranged over two floors and retains much of its traditional charm. On the ground floor, a welcoming living room is centred around a classic Stanley stove with back boiler, providing heat to both the radiators and hot water system, creating a warm and efficient heart to the home. The dining room and kitchen are located to the rear of the property. To the gable end, a sunroom provides additional living space and enjoys pleasant views over the surrounding countryside. The house would benefit from some upgrading and modernisation. There is potential to create a bright and attractive extension to the living accommodation. \n\nUpstairs, the property comprises 2 bedrooms and a family bathroom. The house offers comfortable accommodation with excellent potential for further enhancement and personalisation.\n\nExternally, the residence stands on a generous site of approximately 0.81 of an acre and benefits from a polytunnel, ideal for gardening enthusiasts, hobby growers or those seeking a more sustainable lifestyle. The grounds abut the nearby Glengarriff river. The services include a gravity-fed fresh water well and a septic tank. \n\nThe location adjacent to the Glengarriff National Park, Barley Lake and within the scenic Caha mountain range, presents a wonderful opportunity for a purchaser to create a charming country home. Combining character, privacy and immense potential with a truly spectacular West Cork location, this is a rare opportunity to acquire a traditional farmhouse within easy reach of both Glengarriff and Kenmare.\n\nDisclaimer:Whilst every care has been taken in the preparation of these particulars, all information is provided in good faith and is believed to be correct, but is not guaranteed. Interested parties should satisfy themselves as to the accuracy and completeness of all details by independent inspection or enquiry. No representation or warranty is made regarding the condition, measurements, boundaries, planning status, services or other information relating to the property. All measurements, maps, photographs and distances are approximate and for guidance purposes only. Photographs, video and drone imagery are provided for illustrative purposes and may include features, furnishings or items not included in the sale."
